---
/**
 * /compare — honest positioning against the tools people already know.
 *
 * Two rules, deliberately stricter than the rest of the site:
 *  1. Every claim about Varve must already appear (in substance) elsewhere
 *     on the site or in the README/llms.txt — nothing new is asserted here.
 *  2. Claims about other products are limited to long-stable, easily
 *     verified category facts (platform, license type, primary focus) —
 *     never pricing specifics or feature-parity claims, which change
 *     independently of this page and would go stale silently. See the
 *     disclaimer section for the same point made to readers.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath, siteUrl } from '../lib/siteUrl';
import ClosingCTA from '../components/ClosingCTA.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Can I use Varve without an account or internet?',
    a: 'Yes. Varve requires no account, no cloud sync, and no internet connection for core editing. Optional network features — model downloads, font search, update checks — are each explicit and user-controlled. Documents are local files on your disk.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Varve a Figma alternative?',
    a: "It's a genuine alternative for vector, layout, typography, and prototyping work, with the opposite storage model: Varve documents are local files with no account required, where Figma is browser-based and built around real-time multi-user collaboration. Varve also runs natively on Linux, which Figma does not. Varve does not have real-time collaboration yet, so if that's central to your workflow, it isn't a drop-in replacement today.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Varve like Adobe Illustrator?',
    a: "Both do vector illustration. Illustrator is desktop software distributed through Adobe's Creative Cloud application suite; Varve is a single free application (vector, layout, typography, motion, and print together) under a source-available license, with no subscription and no account requirement.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Varve like Affinity Designer, Photo, or Publisher?',
    a: "Similar in spirit — desktop-native, not subscription-dependent for core use — but Affinity ships as separate apps for vector, raster, and publishing work, while Varve combines vector, layout, typography, motion, prototyping, and print in one document model and one application.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How is Varve different from Inkscape or Penpot?',
    a: 'Inkscape and Penpot are both free and open source, so the free-to-use ground is shared. Varve differs in scope (layout, typography, motion, and print production alongside vector editing, in one document model) and in license: Varve is source-available under FSL-1.1-MIT, not OSI-approved open source, though each release converts to plain MIT two years after it ships.',
  },
  {
    q: "Should I switch to Varve today?",
    a: "Only if beta software is an acceptable trade for what it offers now. Varve is public beta: interfaces and the .varve document format can still change, and Windows/macOS builds are not yet code-signed. It's a reasonable choice for exploring a local-first workflow or testing whether the combined toolset fits you; it is not yet the right choice for a deadline you can't afford to miss.",
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(({ q, a }) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const pageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': `${siteUrl('/compare')}#webpage`,
  url: siteUrl('/compare'),
  name: 'Compare Varve to other design tools',
  description:
    'How Varve differs from Figma, Adobe Illustrator, Affinity, Sketch, Inkscape, and Penpot on pricing, platform, license, and collaboration.',
  inLanguage: 'en',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Compare Varve to Other Design Tools"
  description="How Varve compares to Figma, Illustrator, Affinity, Sketch, Inkscape, and Penpot on pricing, platform, license, and collaboration — compared honestly."
  structuredData={[pageSchema, faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="compare-page">
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">How Varve compares</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">
        There's no single best design tool — only a better or worse fit for how you work. This
        page is the honest version: what actually differs, and where Varve currently falls short
        for people coming from something else.
      </p>

      <section class="compare-section">
        <h2>What to weigh, regardless of what you're switching from</h2>
        <p>These are facts about Varve itself — the same ones on the <a href={sitePath('/product')}>product overview</a> and in the <a href={sitePath('/support/faq')}>FAQ</a>, gathered in one table.</p>
        <div class="spec-table" role="table" aria-label="Varve at a glance">
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">Price</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Free. No subscription, no feature paywall (Community Edition).</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">Account</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">None required. Core editing works fully offline.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">Where files live</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Local disk (desktop) or local browser storage (web build). No mandatory cloud sync.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">Platforms</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Native desktop app on Linux, Windows (x86_64 and ARM64), and macOS (Apple Silicon). No hosted web editor yet.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">License</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Source-available, FSL-1.1-MIT — each release converts to plain MIT two years after it ships.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">Collaboration</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Not implemented yet — UI scaffolding only, single-user today.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row" role="row">
            <span class="spec-key" role="columnheader">Maturity</span>
            <span class="spec-val" role="cell">Public beta — interfaces and the .varve format can still change.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="compare-section">
        <h2>Category facts at a glance</h2>
        <p class="compare-sub">Long-stable facts from each tool's public documentation. Pricing changes frequently — verify current details on each product's own site.</p>
        <div class="compare-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Design tool comparison">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col"></th>
                <th scope="col">Varve</th>
                <th scope="col">Figma</th>
                <th scope="col">Illustrator</th>
                <th scope="col">Affinity</th>
                <th scope="col">Inkscape</th>
                <th scope="col">Penpot</th>
                <th scope="col">Sketch</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Linux</th>
                <td>Native</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td>Native</td>
                <td>Browser</td>
                <td>No</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Native desktop</th>
                <td>Yes</td>
                <td>Mac, Windows</td>
                <td>Mac, Windows</td>
                <td>Mac, Windows, iPad</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td>Mac only</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">License</th>
                <td>Source-available<sup>[1]</sup></td>
                <td>Proprietary</td>
                <td>Proprietary</td>
                <td>Proprietary</td>
                <td>GPL-2.0+</td>
                <td>MPL-2.0</td>
                <td>Proprietary</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Collaboration</th>
                <td>Single-user</td>
                <td>Real-time</td>
                <td>File-based</td>
                <td>File-based</td>
                <td>Single-user</td>
                <td>Real-time</td>
                <td>File-based</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Storage</th>
                <td>Local files</td>
                <td>Cloud account</td>
                <td>Local files</td>
                <td>Local files</td>
                <td>Local files</td>
                <td>Cloud account</td>
                <td>Local files</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="compare-table-note">[1] Varve is source-available under FSL-1.1-MIT; each release converts to MIT after two years. Varve does not cover every task these established tools handle — it trades breadth-of-maturity for a single-document, cross-discipline model.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="compare-section">
        <h2>If you're coming from&hellip;</h2>
        <div class="from-grid">
          <div class="from-card">
            <h3>Figma</h3>
            <p class="from-what">Browser-based, built around real-time multi-user collaboration and UI design workflows.</p>
            <p class="from-diff"><strong>Varve differs:</strong> a native desktop app with documents as local files, no account — and it runs natively on Linux, which Figma does not. No real-time collaboration yet.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="from-card">
            <h3>Adobe Illustrator</h3>
            <p class="from-what">Desktop vector illustration software, part of the wider Adobe Creative Cloud application suite.</p>
            <p class="from-diff"><strong>Varve differs:</strong> one application that also covers layout, typography, motion, and print — not a suite of separate apps.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="from-card">
            <h3>Affinity (Designer, Photo, Publisher)</h3>
            <p class="from-what">Desktop vector, raster, and publishing apps, now part of Canva's Affinity line.</p>
            <p class="from-diff"><strong>Varve differs:</strong> vector, raster, layout, and publishing live in one document model instead of three separate apps.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="from-card">
            <h3>Sketch</h3>
            <p class="from-what">A macOS-only UI design tool.</p>
            <p class="from-diff"><strong>Varve differs:</strong> cross-platform — Linux, macOS, and Windows from the same codebase.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="from-card">
            <h3>Inkscape</h3>
            <p class="from-what">Free, open-source, cross-platform vector editor licensed under the GPL.</p>
            <p class="from-diff"><strong>Varve differs:</strong> adds layout, typography, motion, prototyping, and print production alongside vector editing; the license is source-available (FSL-1.1-MIT), not GPL.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="from-card">
            <h3>Penpot</h3>
            <p class="from-what">Free, open-source, browser-based design and prototyping tool.</p>
            <p class="from-diff"><strong>Varve differs:</strong> a native desktop app rather than browser-based, with print production and offline-first storage.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="compare-disclaimer">
          Varve is an independent project, not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
          Figma, Adobe, Canva/Affinity, Sketch, Inkscape, or Penpot. Names are trademarks of
          their respective owners. Pricing and feature details for those products change
          independently of this page — verify current specifics on their own sites; what's
          verified here is Varve's own.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="compare-section">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          {faqs.map(({ q, a }) => (
            <div class="faq-item">
              <h3>{q}</h3>
              <p>{a}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <ClosingCTA
        title="See it yourself"
        accentWord="for free."
        text="Free and source-available under FSL-1.1-MIT. Public beta — expect rough edges."
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .compare-page {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 0;
  }

  .compare-page .page-hero-title {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .compare-page .page-hero-sub {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .compare-section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .compare-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .compare-section > p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .compare-section > p a {
    color: var(--text-link);
  }

  .compare-section > p a:hover {
    color: var(--text-link-hover);
  }

  .spec-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .spec-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(140px, 0.8fr) 2fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .spec-row + .spec-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }

  .spec-row:nth-child(odd) {
    background: var(--surface-card);
  }

  .spec-key {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .spec-val {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .from-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(260px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .from-card {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .from-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .from-what {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .from-diff {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .from-diff strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .compare-disclaimer {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 68ch;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .faq-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .faq-item p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .compare-table-wrap {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  }

  .compare-table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 680px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .compare-table th,
  .compare-table td {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .compare-table thead th {
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
  }

  .compare-table thead th:first-child {
    background: var(--surface-card);
  }

  .compare-table tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    background: var(--surface-card);
  }

  .compare-table tbody tr:hover td,
  .compare-table tbody tr:hover th {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--surface-sunken) 70%, var(--surface-card));
  }

  .compare-table-note {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .compare-sub {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .spec-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
